Bricker Game (EX2)

An Arkanoid-style 2D arcade game built in Java using DanoGameLab.
The player moves a paddle to deflect the ball, break all bricks,
and manage lives while triggering special brick behaviors.

Architecture & Design:
- Game Objects (bricker.gameobjects):
  Ball, PuckBall, Paddle, ExtraPaddle (disappears after 4 hits),
  Brick, ExtraHeart, and Hearts (UI icons + color-coded counter).
- Collision Strategies (bricker.brick_strategies):
  Implemented via CollisionStrategy with access to GameObjectCollection
  for self-contained object management.
- Special Behaviors:
  - BasicCollisionStrategy: Removes the brick and decrements the counter.
  - AddPucksStrategy: Spawns two smaller, faster PuckBalls in random directions.
  - ExtraPaddleStrategy: Spawns a temporary center paddle (max one active).
  - ExplodeNeighborsStrategy: Destroys adjacent bricks with sound effects.
  - HeartCollisionStrategy: Drops an ExtraHeart that adds a life (up to 4)
    when caught by the main paddle.
  - MultipleStrategy: Combines up to 3 strategies on one brick via
    FactoryOfStrategies whilee preventing infinite nesting.
